 "forecast_note": "Not in these lines: the pending Adonai Mitchell for Josh Downs claim (Wed 2:00 AM, priority 12 of 13, a breakout claim that The Winners and Waiting for Gordon can take first). If it lands, Downs' line is void and Mitchell is unforecast. Bands are the library's widths: the q75 rebuild test written for 11-03 was not run (it needs an interactive session), so the week 7 alarm stays open.",
 "review_note": "Won 164.8 to 86.4 against End-Zone Dancers. Coverage this week: 50% 0.36, 90% 0.86 (n=14); baseline 0.43 and 1.00. Season: 50% 0.49, 90% 0.93 (n=110), inside the 0.50 +/- 0.12 alarm band. WIS: MIST 3.21, baseline 3.26 (difference -0.05, se 0.10). Closing line value: corr 0.188, sign agreement 0.50 on 40 moves. FantasyPros ranks: week 9 MIST minus ECR +4.2 (worse), 3-week mean +7.0. Landing slices: q75-q95 at 35% against a calibrated 20%, at the alarm level for the second time (37% after week 7). The high side is where we miss: Walker 36.3, Chase 31.5 and Christian Watson 30.1 all landed above the 50% band, and Watson above the 90% (0-15.5 / 0-27, the questionable mixture at 0.71 to play cut his top). Judged as variance inside well-shaped bands for Walker and Chase. Watson is a band-shape issue: a zero-or-line mixture pulls the upper quantiles down, and that is the second candidate cause of the q75-q95 excess beside the tier medians under 1.0. No rule change from one week: the q75 rebuild test still waits on an interactive session. Opponent 86.4 landed at the 90% floor (Burrow and Gibbs low), variance."
